  "description": "This program is available at the following location: Corvallis Options available: Forest Management Forest Operations Management Forest Restoration and Fire The successful forester must understand the biological and physical processes of forest ecosystems, as well as the social, economic, and operational forces that influence forest policies and management actions. The forestry core curriculum includes basic courses in the biological, physical, social sciences, and six months of work experience as well as professional courses designed to prepare students to manage forest resources. Students are required to select one of the following required options: Forest Restoration and Fire Forest Management Forest Operations Management The Bachelor of Science degree in Forestry is accredited by the Society of American Foresters (SAF). Major Code: 820 Pre-Forestry Major Code: 810",
